<title>Approximating a nonlinear function by a linear function</title>

<p><ref>Video</ref> | <ref>Summary</ref> | <ref>Transcript</ref>  </p>
<description>
The secant line and tangent line are two ways to approximate a nonlinear function by a linear one.
</description>

<p>Linear functions are nice and easy to deal with.  But, in many cases and applications, one doesn't have a linear function to work with.  Instead, one has a nonlinear function.  One part of calculus can be viewed as approximating nonlinear functions by linear functions.</p>

